1: #!/usr/bin/env python3
2: """i8259_eoi_probe.py -- the DETECTOR (and the re-pinned rung-3 witness) for ledger row `i8259eoiirr` (#574),
3: src/devices/dev_8259.c (+ the GT64120 interrupt-acknowledge read in src/devices/dev_gt.c), on the UNMODIFIED
4: `evbmips -e malta` machine.
5: 
6: THE DEFECT, as the pass-1 brief and its adjudication settled it: the 8259 model had NO interrupt acknowledge.  The
7: OCW3 poll read returned a (mask-blind) poll byte and set no in-service (ISR) bit; the GT64120 IACK read returned the
8: last asserted line and acknowledged nothing; and the SPECIFIC EOI (OCW2 0x60|n) stood in for the missing acknowledge
9: by clearing the REQUEST bit (IRR) of the EOI'd line -- although on the chip an EOI resets an ISR bit only, and the
10: request bit is cleared by the acknowledge.  Two guest-visible consequences on malta: a request a device still holds
11: is dropped by the EOI until the device re-asserts (the one-shot pckbc never does while its queue holds data), and the
12: 8253 timer -- whose pending-event count was never retired, because the only decrement sat in a bus deassert the 8253
13: never issues -- was re-delivered once per 2^14-instruction emulator tick instead of once per programmed period
14: (measured: 7,415 IRQ 0 deliveries in 180M guest instructions at a programmed 18 Hz; rate_explore_20261025/).
15: 
16: THE FIX (design (G'), F2 of pass 1): the acknowledge exists -- `pic8259_acknowledge()` moves the highest-priority
17: unmasked request to service (ISR bit set, IRR bit cleared, the 8253's event retired on pic1 line 0), called by the
18: read after an OCW3 poll (one-shot: later reads return the IRR) and by the GT IACK read; the specific EOI resets the
19: ISR bit when the line is in service and otherwise CONSUMES the request as it always did (the legacy path for machines
20: whose vector read acknowledges nothing: PReP, footbridge); the non-specific EOI resets the lowest set ISR bit.
21: 
22: ORACLE RE-PIN (the oracle-correction rule): the pass-1 witness (witness_20261025/, 19 rows) pinned `eoi irr4` and
23: `eoi x8` as SYMPTOM rows wanting the request bit KEPT after an un-acknowledged EOI.  Under (G') an EOI with no
24: preceding acknowledge keeps the legacy consume, so those two rows are RE-PINNED here as the CONTRACT row `eoi noack`
25: (both columns 0); the symptom rows are the ACKNOWLEDGE rows below.  Each revision of this probe is run on the
26: UNMODIFIED HEAD clone first (HEAD column: witness_20261025b/ for v2, witness_20261025c/ for v2d) and the pre-fix build
27: is measured RED against the FIX column (the L0 leg) before any fix measurement is trusted.  Honest order note: the fix
