69:            instructions with counter 0 at 18 Hz: HEAD >= 5000 (one per tick); FIX 1..1000 (one per host-timer fire).
70: 
71: CONTRACT (clause (e)): CATCHES a reinstated IRR clear in the specific-EOI arm in any form (unconditional; conditioned
72: on the mask, on n != 4, or on the ISR bit -- `eoi acked`, `eoi acked3`, `masked eoi`), a poll that acknowledges
73: nothing or returns a masked line (`poll isr`, `poll irr4`, `poll masked`), a sticky poll latch (`poll once`), a GT
74: read that acknowledges nothing (`gt isr`, `gt irr4`) or returns the legacy line instead of the acknowledged one
75: (`gtboth iack`), an acknowledge that does not retire the 8253's event (`rate
76: storm`/`rate band`), a cascade acknowledge that strands or skips the slave (`casc isr2`, `casc isr8`), a non-specific
77: EOI that clears every ISR bit (`nonspec lowest`).  OUTSIDE: the `default` read arm (byte-identical to HEAD), priority
78: inhibition by ISR (not modelled; filed i8259priority), level-triggered mode (ICW1 LTIM; filed i8259ltim), the PReP
79: and footbridge vector reads (filed isaiackreaders), the OCW2 bytes that stop the emulation (filed i8259cmdhalt), an
80: 8253 count of zero (filed pit8253count0), the spurious IACK with nothing pending (returns last_int, as HEAD).
81: A held level re-requests after the acknowledge within one tick (the model's devices re-assert every tick while a
82: condition holds) -- more generous than edge-mode hardware, never less; disclosed, not rowed.
83: 
84: CONTROLS: every emitted WORD of every guest program is checked against the emulator's own disassembler (CONTROL 0);
85: each session parks at its halt breakpoint with the pc verified; a RAM round-trip through the same store/load shapes
86: (a device row reading 0 can never be blamed on a bad encoding); the level/pending controls (`* irr4`, `casc irr2`,
87: `pit irr0`, `rate delivered`) prove the source is up before a row reads it; `quiet *` is the device signature (a
88: PIC answers 0/0/0x00 where RAM would answer 0x5a).  The leg's CONTROL fails on any red control-kind row, bad word,
89: or wrong park; a red SYMPTOM or CONTRACT row fails the leg (the model changed) and does not fail CONTROL.
90: 
91: SITES (grep anchors): dev_8259.c `pic8259_acknowledge(`, `DEVICE_ACCESS(8259)` (the `idata == 0x20` arm, the
92: `(idata >= 0x21 && idata <= 0x27)` arm, `case 0x0c:` read); dev_gt.c `case GT_PCI0_INTR_ACK:`; devices.h
93: `struct pic8259_data`; bus_isa.c `isa_interrupt_assert(` / `isa_interrupt_deassert(` / `isa_interrupt_common(`;
94: dev_8253.c `DEVICE_TICK(8253)`; machine_evbmips.c `bus_isa_init(machine, tmpstr, 0, 0x18000000`.
95: 
96: TEMPLATE: regress/le_csrmask_probe.py (#573): pty driver, disassembler self-check, raw transcript per session,
97: breakpoint park, row/verdict/sentinel protocol; regress/wdc_lba_probe.py (#572) for the malta machine.
98: 
99: USAGE: i8259_eoi_probe.py <base_bin> <fix_bin | GATE | -> <outdir>
100:     <base> -      <outdir>  WITNESS: one leg (HEAD column)
101:     <base> <fix>  <outdir>  two legs (HEAD column, FIX column)
102:     <bin>  GATE   <outdir>  ONE leg vs the FIX column: I8259EOI_CONTROL=OK|FAIL, I8259EOI_RESULT=p/n
103: The output ends with the sentinel I8259EOI_PROBE_DONE once; raw transcripts under <outdir>/raw/.
104: """
105: import os
106: import pty
107: import re
108: import select
109: import sys
110: import time
111: 
112: BASE_BIN = sys.argv[1] if len(sys.argv) > 1 else "/tmp/gxt19/base/gxemul"
113: FIX_ARG = sys.argv[2] if len(sys.argv) > 2 else "-"
114: OUTDIR = sys.argv[3] if len(sys.argv) > 3 else "/tmp/gxt19/run"
115: GATE = (FIX_ARG == "GATE")
116: RAWDIR = None                      # OUTDIR/raw
117: 
118: MACHINE = ["-E", "evbmips", "-e", "malta"]   # MIPS Malta evaluation board, little-endian, UNMODIFIED
119: BASE = 0xffffffff80100000          # KSEG0, physical 0x00100000 (inside malta's RAM; the #572 probe's address)
120: HANDLER = 0xffffffff80000180       # the MIPS general exception vector with Status.BEV clear (cpu_mips.c: base + 0x180)
121: ISA_HI = 0xb800                    # KSEG1 0xffffffffb8000000 = physical 0x18000000, the ISA I/O window
122: GT_HI = 0xbbe0                     # KSEG1 0xffffffffbbe00000 = the GT64120 (machine_evbmips.c: dev_gt_init at 0x1be00000)
123: GT_IACK = 0x0c34                   # gtreg.h: GT_PCI0_INTR_ACK
124: RAM_HI = 0x8020                    # KSEG0 scratch (physical 0x200000) for RAM liveness
125: RAM_MAGIC = 0x5a
126: PIC1_CMD, PIC1_IMR = 0x20, 0x21
127: PIC2_CMD, PIC2_IMR = 0xa0, 0xa1
128: UART4_IER, UART4_MCR = 0x3f9, 0x3fc        # the first ISA ns16550 (IRQ 4)
129: UART3_IER, UART3_MCR = 0x2f9, 0x2fc        # the second ISA ns16550 (IRQ 3, in_use=0 -- it still interrupts)
130: IER_ETXRDY = 0x02                  # dev_ns16550.c: transmitter-empty interrupt enable
131: MCR_IENABLE = 0x08                 # the OUT2 gate the model requires before asserting
132: PIT_C0, PIT_CTL = 0x40, 0x43
133: CMOS_IDX, CMOS_DAT = 0x70, 0x71    # the ISA pccmos (mc146818) index/data ports
134: OCW3_IRR, OCW3_ISR, OCW3_POLL = 0x0a, 0x0b, 0x0c
135: EOI_NONSPEC = 0x20
136: COP0_STATUS = 12
137: STATUS_IE_IM2 = 0x0401             # IE | IM2 (the ISA bus is on cpu[N].2 -> Cause.IP2; cpu_mips.c line = 1 << (8 + 2))
138: DELAY_ITER = 12000                 # 3 instructions per iteration: ~36k instructions > two UART ticks (2^14 each)
139: LONG_ITER = 6000000                # ~18M instructions per wait; THREE waits before sampling a host-timer source
140:                                    # (the measured-sufficient envelope of timer_explore_20261025)
141: RATE_SPIN = 60000000               # 180M instructions of counting in the rate session
142: 
143: zero, v0, v1, a0, a1, a2, a3 = 0, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7
144: t0, t1, t2, t3, t4, t5, t6, t7 = 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14, 15
145: s0, s1, s2, s3, s4, s5 = 16, 17, 18, 19, 20, 21
146: k0, k1 = 26, 27
147: NAME = {zero: "zr", v0: "v0", v1: "v1", a0: "a0", a1: "a1", a2: "a2", a3: "a3",
148:         t0: "t0", t1: "t1", t2: "t2", t3: "t3", t4: "t4", t5: "t5", t6: "t6", t7: "t7",
149:         s0: "s0", s1: "s1", s2: "s2", s3: "s3", s4: "s4", s5: "s5", k0: "k0", k1: "k1"}
150: 
151: 
152: def I(op, rs, rt, imm):
153:     return (op << 26) | (rs << 21) | (rt << 16) | (imm & 0xffff)
154: 
155: 
156: def R(rs, rt, rd, sa, funct):
157:     return (rs << 21) | (rt << 16) | (rd << 11) | (sa << 6) | funct
158: 
159: 
160: def lui(rt, imm):
161:     return I(0x0F, 0, rt, imm)
162: 
163: 
164: def ori(rt, rs, imm):
165:     return I(0x0D, rs, rt, imm)
166: 
167: 
168: def addiu(rt, rs, imm):
169:     return I(0x09, rs, rt, imm)
170: 
171: 
172: def andi(rt, rs, imm):
173:     return I(0x0C, rs, rt, imm)
174: 
175: 
176: def sb(rt, off, base):
177:     return I(0x28, base, rt, off)
178: 
179: 
180: def lbu(rt, off, base):
181:     return I(0x24, base, rt, off)
182: 
183: 
184: def lw(rt, off, base):
185:     return I(0x23, base, rt, off)
186: 
187: 
188: def beq(rs, rt, off):
189:     return I(0x04, rs, rt, off)
190: 
191: 
192: def bne(rs, rt, off):
193:     return I(0x05, rs, rt, off)
194: 
195: 
196: def or_(rd, rs, rt):
197:     return R(rs, rt, rd, 0, 0x25)
198: 
199: 
200: def mtc0(rt, rd):
201:     return 0x40800000 | (rt << 16) | (rd << 11)
202: 
203: 
204: ERET = 0x42000018
205: NOP = 0
206: prog = []
207: 
208: 
209: def reset_prog():
210:     del prog[:]
211: 
212: 
213: def emit(word, mn):
214:     """mn is checked against the EMULATOR'S OWN disassembly (CONTROL 0): the word is the authoritative check, the
215:     mnemonic a rendering counted separately."""
216:     prog.append((word, mn))
217: 
218: 
219: def e_li(rt, v):
220:     emit(ori(rt, zero, v), "ori %s,zr,0x%x" % (NAME[rt], v & 0xffff))
221: 
222: 
223: def e_out(port, v, tmp=t3):
224:     """Byte store of v to ISA port: ori tmp,zr,v; sb tmp,port(t0)."""
225:     e_li(tmp, v)
226:     emit(sb(tmp, port, t0), "sb %s,%d(t0)" % (NAME[tmp], port))
227: 
228: 
229: def e_in(rt, port):
230:     emit(lbu(rt, port, t0), "lbu %s,%d(t0)" % (NAME[rt], port))
231: 
232: 
233: def e_ocw3_read(rt, which, cmd=PIC1_CMD):
234:     """Select an OCW3 read register (irr 0x0a / isr 0x0b / poll 0x0c) on a PIC and read it into rt."""
235:     e_out(cmd, which)
236:     e_in(rt, cmd)
237: 
238: 
239: def e_eoi(n, cmd=PIC1_CMD):
240:     e_out(cmd, 0x60 | n)
241: 
242: 
243: def e_uart_level_on(ier=UART4_IER, mcr=UART4_MCR):
244:     """Turn an ISA ns16550 into a steady level source: MCR_IENABLE, then IER_ETXRDY."""
245:     e_out(mcr, MCR_IENABLE)
246:     e_out(ier, IER_ETXRDY)
247: 
248: 
249: def e_delay():
250:     """A counted loop longer than one ns16550 tick: ori t4,zr,N; loop: addiu t4,t4,-1; bne t4,zr,loop; nop."""
251:     e_li(t4, DELAY_ITER)
252:     emit(addiu(t4, t4, -1), "addiu t4,t4,-1")
253:     emit(bne(t4, zero, -2), "bne t4,zr,0x")
254:     emit(NOP, "nop")
255: 
256: 
257: def e_long(n=LONG_ITER):
258:     emit(lui(t4, (n >> 16) & 0xffff), "lui t4,0x%x" % ((n >> 16) & 0xffff))
259:     emit(ori(t4, t4, n & 0xffff), "ori t4,t4,0x%x" % (n & 0xffff))
260:     emit(addiu(t4, t4, -1), "addiu t4,t4,-1")
261:     emit(bne(t4, zero, -2), "bne t4,zr,0x")
262:     emit(NOP, "nop")
263: 
264: 
265: def e_pit_291hz():
266:     """8253 counter 0: control 0x34 (counter 0, LSB+MSB, mode 2), count 0x1000 -> a 291 Hz host timer."""
267:     e_out(PIT_CTL, 0x34)
268:     e_out(PIT_C0, 0x00)
269:     e_out(PIT_C0, 0x10)
270: 
271: 
272: def begin():
273:     """Common preamble: t0 = ISA I/O window, t2 = RAM scratch, and the RAM liveness control (the same sb/lbu shapes
274:     through plain RAM, so a device row reading 0 can never be blamed on a bad encoding): v0 = RAM round-trip."""
275:     reset_prog()
276:     emit(lui(t0, ISA_HI), "lui t0,0x%x" % ISA_HI)
277:     emit(lui(t2, RAM_HI), "lui t2,0x%x" % RAM_HI)
278:     e_li(t3, RAM_MAGIC)
279:     emit(sb(t3, 0, t2), "sb t3,0(t2)")
280:     emit(lbu(v0, 0, t2), "lbu v0,0(t2)")
281: 
282: 
283: def end():
284:     halt = len(prog)
285:     emit(beq(zero, zero, -1), "b 0x")
286:     emit(NOP, "nop")
287:     return list(prog), BASE + halt * 4
288: 
289: 
290: def build_quiet():
291:     begin()
292:     e_ocw3_read(v1, OCW3_IRR)
293:     e_in(a2, PIC1_CMD)
294:     e_ocw3_read(a0, OCW3_ISR)
295:     e_ocw3_read(a1, OCW3_POLL)
296:     e_in(a3, PIC1_IMR)
297:     p, halt = end()
298:     return p, halt, {"ram": "v0", "irr": "v1", "stable": "a2", "isr": "a0", "poll": "a1", "imr": "a3"}, None
299: 
300: 
301: def build_level():
302:     """The UART level on IRQ 4; the un-acknowledged specific EOI (legacy consume, both columns); the re-assert."""
303:     begin()
304:     e_uart_level_on()
305:     e_delay()
306:     e_ocw3_read(v1, OCW3_IRR)
307:     e_in(a2, PIC1_CMD)
308:     e_ocw3_read(a0, OCW3_ISR)
309:     e_li(t5, OCW3_IRR)
310:     e_li(t6, 0x64)
311:     emit(sb(t6, PIC1_CMD, t0), "sb t6,%d(t0)" % PIC1_CMD)
312:     emit(sb(t5, PIC1_CMD, t0), "sb t5,%d(t0)" % PIC1_CMD)
313:     e_in(a1, PIC1_CMD)
314:     e_delay()
315:     e_ocw3_read(a3, OCW3_IRR)
316:     e_ocw3_read(s0, OCW3_ISR)
317:     p, halt = end()
318:     return p, halt, {"ram": "v0", "irr": "v1", "stable": "a2", "isr": "a0", "noack": "a1", "reassert": "a3", "isr2": "s0"}, None
